From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0400: precise guest vblank on Win32 (absolute grid, high-resolution timer, QPC spin, MMCSS)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (W3.2). The idea (absolute grid, a precise wait, a statistics line) is $IOS
  games/mcla/sdk_patches/0208-guest-vblank-grid-stats.patch (+0209) redone for Win32; no code is shared (that one is
  Mach real-time threads and os_sync)
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: Windows: the guest vblank thread fires on an absolute grid of 1/video_mode_refresh_rate seconds from a QPC
  origin (high-resolution waitable timer to ~0.3 ms before each point, QPC spin for the rest), at MMCSS "Games" and
  time-critical priority; a vblank over one period late resyncs the grid (no burst); one
  `[guest-vblank] period p50=.. p99=.. late=.. resync=.. n=..` line every 10 s. Cvars guest_vblank_precise (true),
  guest_vblank_spin_us (300). vsync=false keeps the SDK loop (warns once). Not built before the first W3 build.
Bucket: REDO

0400-guest-vblank-precise-win32.patch (mcla-x86 W3.2; redoes the idea of $IOS 0208/0209 for Windows)

Purpose. The SDK's vblank thread (GraphicsSystem::SetupGuestGpu, "GPU VSync") wakes every Sleep(1 ms), measures the
elapsed guest ticks against the period and replays every vblank it finds due. On Windows that is a guest vblank that
lands 0-2 ms after its time (Sleep granularity and a normal-priority thread) and, after a late wake, two vblanks in a
row: the game's frame pacer sees a period wandering over ~15-18 ms. The first guest frame of a 60 Hz lock can only be as
steady as this clock.

Change (src/graphics/graphics_system.cpp, Windows only; the other platforms' code is byte-identical):
  * class PreciseVblank (anonymous namespace). An absolute grid: point n is origin + n * qpc_hz / refresh_rate, the
    origin one QueryPerformanceCounter reading (re-taken when the loop engages and on a resync). Each wait: a
    CREATE_WAITABLE_TIMER_HIGH_RESOLUTION timer to (point - guest_vblank_spin_us - overshoot), then YieldProcessor
    spinning on QPC to the point. `overshoot` is the largest lateness of the timer's last 64 wakes, capped at 1.5 ms,
    so a timer that wakes 0.4 ms late costs a longer spin, not a late vblank. No high-resolution timer (Windows older
    than 10 1803): Sleep(1) to 3 ms before the point, then the spin.
  * Late handling: a vblank that is less than one period late fires at once and the grid stays (the next point is on
    time); more than one period late re-anchors the grid on now and fires once (resync counted), the missed vblanks
    are never replayed. The period follows Clock::guest_time_scalar() (guest time), a change starts a new grid.
  * The vblank thread engages on its first precise wait: SetThreadPriority(TIME_CRITICAL) first, then
    AvSetMmThreadCharacteristicsW(L"Games") (MMCSS manages the thread afterwards); both are undone when the loop goes
    back to the SDK's, or the thread ends. Both outcomes are logged (`[guest-vblank] precise grid: ...`).
  * Cvar guest_vblank_precise (GPU, bool, default true, live; false = the SDK's loop as before). With vsync=false the
    SDK's loop is kept untouched (the guest vblank fires every 1 ms, as before) and a warning says so once.
  * Statistics: `[guest-vblank] period p50=<ms> p99=<ms> late=<n> resync=<n> n=<count>` every 10 s (nearest-rank
    percentiles of the periods between the QPC stamps taken when each vblank fired, ms with 3 decimals; late = periods
    over 1.05x nominal; n = periods in the window). The SDK's own loop (guest_vblank_precise=false, vsync=false) feeds
    the same line, for an A/B of the two.
  * src/graphics/CMakeLists.txt: rexgpu-xenos links avrt on Windows.

Not built or run (clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only of the TU with the SDK's Release flags: no new diagnostics).
Verify: `[guest-vblank] precise grid: 60.000 Hz ... MMCSS Games joined ... time-critical priority set` at start-up, then
p50 16.66-16.68, p99 <= 17.2, resync 0 in a steady 60 fps scene; A/B with --guest_vblank_precise=false.

